<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Divashtich</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 722</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Divashtich was the ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/panjikent">Panjikent</a> in Sogdiana who in the early 720s claimed the titles king of Sogdiana and lord of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samarkand">Samarkand</a>. Resisting the Umayyad Arab conquest, he retreated to the castle on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-mugh">Mount Mugh</a>, where he was captured in 722 and crucified. His archive of documents in Sogdian, found at Mount Mugh in 1932–1933, is a key source on Sogdian society.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/divashtich.jpg" alt="Divashtich" width="320" height="465" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ALFGRN · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Possible_Sogdian_King_Devashtish_or_God_Verethranga,_Aini_district,_Tajikistan,_7-8th_century_CE,_National_Museum_of_Antiquities_of_Tajikistan_(A_1060).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
